
Main heading:  Calm World

Tagline: Simple free mindfulness practices anyone on Earth can use today.

Intro paragraph: Stress doesn’t respect borders. In every country, millions of people are looking for a moment of calm. These universal techniques come from tradition all over the planet and need nothing but a few quiet minutes no apps, no cost, no experience required.


Page heading: 10 Daily Practices You Can Do Anywhere

1. 4-7-8 Breathing Inhale for 4 seconds, hold for 7, exhale for 8. Repeat four times.
2. One-Minute Body Scan Close your eyes and slowly notice each part of your body from toes to head.
3. Gratitude Pause  Name three things you’re thankful for right now.
4. Five-Finger Grounding  Look for 5 things you can see, 4 you can touch, 3 you can hear, 2 you can smell, 1 you can taste.
5. Walking Meditation Walk slowly, feeling each foot touch the ground.
6. Loving-Kindness Phrases  Silently repeat: “May I be safe. May I be healthy. May I live with ease.”
7. Sky Gazing  Look up at the sky or ceiling for 60 seconds and let thoughts drift like clouds.
8. Shoulder Roll & Neck Stretch  Gently roll shoulders and tilt head side to side for 30 seconds.
9. Hand-on-Heart Place one hand on your heart, breathe deeply, and feel warmth.
10. Smile for No Reason Gently smile for 15 seconds — the brain responds as if you’re happy.


Page heading: Mindfulness Traditions From Six Continents

Japan Forest Bathing (Shinrin-yoku)
Spend time among trees, breathing deeply. Proven to lower stress hormones.

India  Nadi Shodhana (Alternate Nostril Breathing)
Balances the nervous system in under two minutes.

Brazil Earthing
Walk barefoot on grass or sand to reconnect with the Earth’s energy.

Scandinavia  Hygge Mindfulness
Light a candle, wrap in a blanket, and fully enjoy the moment of cosiness.

Morocco  Mint Tea Ritual
Brew and drink mint tea slowly, making the simple act a meditation.

Tibet / Global  Loving-Kindness (Metta)
Send silent wishes of peace to yourself, loved ones, and all beings everywhere.

